"toolu_01RYc3Pj2dTYA8oX1K9cEW93", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 28376, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. Its error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%, and the service now shows as healthy.\n\n1. **Which service:** There's no service called just \"payments,\" so I tried a few likely names. payments-api is the one that exists and was failing: it was running v5.1.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), marked unhealthy, with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Which version to go back to:** Its release history has only two production releases: v5.0.0 (healthy) and v5.1.0 (degraded, this morning's deploy). That makes v5.0.0 the most recent healthy release.\n3. **Rollback:** v5.0.0 is now live in all three regions.\n4. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** as a SEV2 for payments-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. The incident says v5.1.0 caused the errors and that we rolled back to v5.0.0.\n\nI couldn't get a list of all services, so I only checked names I guessed. If another payments service was also changed in this morning's deploy, I haven't checked it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BFgCZQiUUs3Jm8cJsAwqhM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016PWGAvRGQ4ssw8wWaQZDxv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PG93bw5YPGxkrKGWxqEKTJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu